  "report_discrepancies": [],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental funds from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p5, Total Governmental Funds column); balance used for roll-forward is fund balance (64,035 to 92,215), which differs from governmental cash assets (94,772) by liabilities of 2,557. Business-type from the proprietary funds statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (p7): receipts = sales + misc + interest; disbursements = operating expenses + capital outlay + debt principal and interest (nonoperating lines, which are cash disbursements); transfers out 10,000 (net position roll: 377,287 + 199,042 - 168,423 - 10,000 = 397,906). No single total revenues printed for business-type, summed. Governmental transfers in 36,267 / out 26,267 net 10,000 (net 10,000 also appears as business transfers). Balance sheet (attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the Balance Sheet - Governmental Funds Total column (p4), whose totals equal the government-wide governmental figures (assets 94,772, liabilities 2,557, fund balance 92,215) with no capital assets, debt or interfund amounts; fund balance by classification (Assigned: Cemetery upkeep 509 is the government-wide 'Unrestricted'). Business-type lines and printed totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail (attempt 2, user per-fund rule 2026-10-27): the only supplementary schedule is the combined All Funds budgetary comparison (p9), so its lines were removed and detail is one line per individual fund column of the governmental funds statement (p5: General, Street, Sales Tax, Keno) and the proprietary funds statement (p7: Water, Sewer, Trash); Total columns not used; budget_final null. Proprietary nonoperating lines (interest income, capital outlay, debt principal/interest) and transfers are printed below the funds' operating totals and carry outside_printed_total. Statement of cash flows (p8) not used since the basis is modified cash (proprietary field null). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
